{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor p in ['/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_020/build_response.json']:\n try:\n  d=json.load(open(p))\n  print(d.get('help','')[:3000])\n  print(json.dumps(d.get('state_inputs'), indent=2))\n except Exception as e: print(e)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor p in ['/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_020/build_response.json']:\n try:\n  d=json.load(open(p))\n  print(d.get('help','')[:3000])\n  print(json.dumps(d.get('state_inputs'), indent=2))\n except Exception as e: print(e)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"<p><strong>What it does</strong></p>\n<p>This tool joins two tabular files based on a common key column.</p>\n<hr class=\"docutils\" />\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<p><strong>First file</strong>:</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nFruit       Color\nApple       red\nBanana      yellow\nOrange      orange\nMelon       green\n</pre>\n<p><strong>Second File</strong>:</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nFruit       Price\nOrange      7\nAvocado     8\nApple       4\nBanana      3\n</pre>\n<p><strong>Joining</strong> both files, using <strong>key column 1</strong> and a <strong>header line</strong>, will return:</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nFruit       Color   Price\nApple       red     4\nAvocado     .       8\nBanana      yellow  3\nMelon       green   .\nOrange      orange  7\n</pre>\n<ul class=\"infomark simple\">\n<li>Input files need not be sorted.</li>\n<li>The header line (<strong>Fruit  Color  Price</strong>) was joined and kept as first line.</li>\n<li>Missing values ( Avocado's color, missing from the first file ) are replaced with a period character.</li>\n</ul>\n\n{\n  \"column1\": \"1\",\n  \"column2\": \"1\",\n  \"empty_string_filler\": \"0\",\n  \"header\": false,\n  \"ignore_case\": false,\n  \"infile1\": {\n    \"values\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721354aa4567590f7f10e\",\n        \"src\": \"hda\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"infile2\": {\n    \"values\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721354aa4567590f7f10e\",\n        \"src\": \"hda\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"jointype\": \" \"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_011/build_response.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint(d.get('help','')[:5000])\nprint('state', json.dumps(d.get('state_inputs'), indent=2)[:3000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_011/build_response.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nprint(d.get('help','')[:5000])\nprint('state', json.dumps(d.get('state_inputs'), indent=2)[:3000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"<p>Use this tool when each selected column is a feature, such as a gene, and you\nneed one Spearman or Pearson correlation test per feature with multiple-testing\ncorrection such as Benjamini-Hochberg FDR.</p>\n<p>Rows are observations and observation rows are matched by the selected\nidentifier columns. For matrices with headers, feature columns are matched by\nheader name. For matrices without headers, selected feature columns are matched\nby ordinal position after the first feature column, and the selected feature\ncounts must match.</p>\n<p>Missing values are dropped separately for each feature, so a feature can still\nbe tested when only some observation pairs are missing. The per-feature p-values\nare adjusted with the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure.</p>\n\nstate {\n  \"alpha\": \"0.05\",\n  \"alternative\": \"two-sided\",\n  \"delimiter_a\": \"tab\",\n  \"delimiter_b\": \"tab\",\n  \"feature_start_a\": \"2\",\n  \"feature_start_b\": \"2\",\n  \"has_header_a\": true,\n  \"has_header_b\": true,\n  \"id_column_a\": \"1\",\n  \"id_column_b\": \"1\",\n  \"matrix_a\": {\n    \"values\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a472135ee7f1d94cfc20184\",\n        \"src\": \"hda\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_b\": {\n    \"values\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a472135ee7f1d94cfc20184\",\n        \"src\": \"hda\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"method\": \"spearman\",\n  \"min_pairs\": \"3\",\n  \"transform_a\": \"none\",\n  \"transform_b\": \"none\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
